One more design consideration on the repaired predicate's `solvesPDE` shape. I want it to be exactly the conjugate-heat equation with the genuine derivative. The unscaled conjugate heat operator is `□* u = -∂_t u - Δu + Ru`. Setting `□* K(·,y,t) = 0` gives `∂_t K(x,y,t) = -Δ_x K(·,y,t) + R(x) K(x,y,t)`. So:
